# VI / EMAcs (cmdref: Session & Files): the command token AS TYPED becomes the editor command, run on
# the file name through the shell, and the CLI waits for it.  'ema' (the 3-character match) is not a
# program, so the shell says so and the prompt returns -- the dispatch and the wait, without an editor.
# 'vi' is real: the "file name" +q! makes vi quit at once (vi's +command form), and the CLI continues.
ema
$TMP/edit_me.txt
vi
+q!
! echo after-vi
# EXPECT: MACOS> ema\s+Enter filename \[no default\]: \S+/edit_me\.txt\s+sh: (1: )?ema: (command )?not found
# EXPECT: MACOS> vi\s+Enter filename \[no default\]: \+q!
# EXPECT: after-vi
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
